 pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","language":"en-GB","onset":"2026-08-26T02:00:00+00:00","parameter":[{"value":"2; Yellow; Moderate","valueName":"awareness_level"},{"value":"3; Thunderstorm","valueName":"awareness_type"},{"value":"There is a small chance that homes and businesses could be flooded quickly, with damage to some buildings from floodwater, lightning strikes or hail","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Where flooding or lightning strikes occur, there is a chance of delays and some cancellations to train and bus services","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Spray and sudden flooding could lead to difficult driving conditions and some road closures","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"There is a slight chance that power cuts could occur and other services to some homes and businesses could be lost","valueName":"impacts"}],"responseType":["Prepare"],"senderName":"UK Met Office","severity":"Moderate","urgency":"Immediate","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings"}],"msgType":"Update","references":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings,2.49.0.0.826.0.GB_260825083123_cef44eaa.v1.0.T,2026-08-25T08:31:23+00:00","scope":"Public","sender":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","sent":"2026-08-26T08:43:35+00:00","source":"2.49.0.0.826.0.GB","status":"Actual"},"raw_properties":{"supersededByAlertId":null,"supersededAt":null,"supersedeType":null,"geometryDescription":"geometry is bbox only, link (member of the feature's links array) with type application/geo+json points to geojson describing the exact shape","geometryType":"bbox","OBJECTID":"e0e2ba67-6c83-45f3-994a-f747cbe3e5bc","alertId":"ebb8438e-91d0-4012-bedb-5c55c2e5fc17","countryCode":"UK","featureType":"polygon","hubLanguage":"en-GB","indexArea":0,"indexFeature":0,"indexInfo":0,"hubTime":"2026-08-26T08:44:45Z","hubLink":"https://meteo.fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com/api/archive/warnings/ebb8438e-91d0-4012-bedb-5c55c2e5fc17.xml?AWSAccessKeyId=DO00LYPLJBWUUWC6D6NU&Expires=1787745324&Signature=j5%2Bb1jo%2ByFzU9VrrKj3RvY3SO0U%3D"}},{"alert_id":"meteo_be35559c-e229-45be-ad01-8bb84abda285","source":"ukmetoffice","title":"Yellow thunderstorm warning","description":"Information on update: Warning extending further NW and to cover all of Wales while removing from parts of the east of England. Matrix position changed to Low likelihood of Medium impacts. A broad band of thunderstorms and heavy rain will move north across England and Wales, perhaps becoming slow moving in the afternoon and evening. Accumulations of 20-30 mm in three hours can be expected fairly widely and up to 50 mm in a 12 hour period can be expected in places. There is a small chance that some places may see more than 50 mm in three hours and more than 75 mm through 12 hours, especially over east facing high ground. Lightning and hail of 1-2 cm will also be hazards and, in a very few places, strong gusts may also present a hazard, these most likely in the south of England early on Thursday morning. \n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","instruction":"Consider if your location is at risk of flash flooding. If so, consider preparing a flood plan and an emergency flood kit.\n\nPrepare to protect your property and people from injury. Before gusty winds arrive, check to ensure moveable objects or temporary structures are well secured. Items include: bins, garden furniture, trampolines, tents, gazebos, sheds, and fences.\n\nGive yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","headline":"Thunderstorms and heavy rain may lead to some disruption: UPDATED","area_desc":"East Midlands | East of England | London & South East England | North West England | South West England | Wales | West Midlands | Yorkshire & Humber","severity":"moderate","certainty":"possible","urgency":"future","tag":["thunderstorm"],"start_date":"2026-08-27T05:00:00+00:00","end_date":"2026-08-27T21:00:00+00:00","geometry":{"coordinates":[[[-3.6127,51.3423],[-3.6733,51.3469],[-3.7341,51.3531],[-3.7951,51.3607],[-3.8565,51.3695],[-3.9183,51.3794],[-3.9807,51.3901],[-4.0436,51.4014],[-4.1072,51.4131],[-4.1715,51.4251],[-4.2367,51.4372],[-4.3028,51.4491],[-4.3699,51.4606],[-4.4382,51.4716],[-4.5076,51.4818],[-4.5977,51.4924],[-4.6987,51.501],[-4.8081,51.5083],[-4.923,51.5146],[-5.041,51.5205],[-5.1594,51.5266],[-5.2754,51.5333],[-5.3866,51.5412],[-5.4902,51.5509],[-5.5837,51.5627],[-5.6643,51.5773],[-5.7294,51.5952],[-5.7765,51.6169],[-5.8028,51.6429],[-5.8058,51.6763],[-5.7847,51.716],[-5.7428,51.7609],[-5.6832,51.81],[-5.6089,51.8624],[-5.5232,51.9171],[-5.4292,51.9732],[-5.33,52.0297],[-5.2288,52.0857],[-5.1287,52.1401],[-5.0328,52.1922],[-4.9443,52.2409],[-4.8663,52.2853],[-4.8019,52.3245],[-4.7654,52.3466],[-4.7269,52.